In article <jdrukman.752979972@dlsun87>, jdrukman%dlsun87@oracle.com (Jon Drukman) writes:
>mgk2r@Virginia.EDU (Michael G. Kurilla) writes:
>>My question would be if some article of armor is already rust-
>>or fireproofed would you still need to remove it before reading?
>
>my test in wizard mode says: yes.  it is perfectly possible for the
>scroll to work on an already proofed piece of armor.  you don't lose
>the proofing that's already there, but you basically waste the scroll.

I think the question was a little more subtle than that.  Suppose you've
got two pieces of armor, one rustproof, one not.  Do you have to remove
the rustproof one to ensure the non-rustproof one gets the rustproofing 
effect.

The answer in that case is no.  It just picks a piece of armor at random,
so a previously rustproof piece of armor may well be selected.
